(import :clan/poo/object)
(export DesignReadings)
(def DesignReadings (.o inspections: (list (.o identity: 'reading-0c03acfc10aa view: 'durable-feature-composition revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-4c42c93ea86e5a4fab072a94c883135f4fc9161097fecd2577c4a303f23c5996 image-sha: "0c03acfc10aad76e0ff0d48a4a4b5ae4ab3f52a5042048617d5ac5c6eef28618" question: 'how-context-is-extended producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the final exported PNG after the spacing change. Each of the five saved fields has a separate, legible line. The dividers distinguish the Feature information, Durable contract information, and checkpoint schema. The restart note points to the binding Core resolves now, and the no-match note keeps the original Attempt open because its checkpoint depends on that binding. The design also allows explicit migration, which this overview leaves to the accompanying text. The right-hand annotations are still denser than the left-hand inputs. This is an observation of the final image.\n")
 (.o identity: 'reading-420e9f463c38 view: 'durable-feature-composition revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-4c42c93ea86e5a4fab072a94c883135f4fc9161097fecd2577c4a303f23c5996 image-sha: "420e9f463c38e8c392881836f85c51b40c94a6c89b62c17d9f421c1f6a8cf405" question: 'how-context-is-extended producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the exported PNG. The folded sheet labeled Saved binding is an identifiable record. It lists Recovery Feature revision, Selected options, Durable provider, Contract version, and Checkpoint schema. The After restart note identifies the other side of the comparison as the binding Core resolves now. The No match note explains why the original Attempt stays open: its checkpoint needs the original binding. Together those clues answer the previous reading's questions about what is saved and what a mismatch changes. A learner may still need checkpoint schema explained as the format used to read the saved state. The annotations keep both restart conditions near the record, with slightly denser text there than on the left. This is a reading of the actual image; it does not measure a learner's comprehension.\n")
 (.o identity: 'reading-098ebb787017 view: 'durable-feature-composition revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-4c42c93ea86e5a4fab072a94c883135f4fc9161097fecd2577c4a303f23c5996 image-sha: "098ebb787017c67537513b0c16b8262c86d73b325b4af266599cc929b69adf31" question: 'how-context-is-extended producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the exported English PNG. At lower left the Recovery tab is already attached to Context and declares needs Durable. At upper left the independent Durable module supplies the contract. The two paths meet at Core, where needs and offers are compared by name and version. The right-hand Context retains its Recovery tab and now carries a saved binding alongside the checkpoint. The attached After restart note explains why the old binding matters before reading the checkpoint. The paths and three main areas are readable. A learner could still ask what the saved binding contains and what happens when no matching provider exists. The visible note does not answer those questions. The source design gives the retained Feature revision, options, provider, contract version and checkpoint schema, and keeps the Attempt unresolved if matching fails. The figure presents the successful binding path, with the mismatch branch left for a separate explanation. This is an actual model reading, with no claim about a learner's response.\n")
 (.o identity: 'reading-52590f44058d view: 'durable-feature-composition revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-058f60b05522ddf968afe1ccb6e4cba711f3c6a4013e5438c88dfeb52b5ac8b5 image-sha: "52590f44058dcf14fb80033f24668f84e3accdaae477ed6c1f4b3d6139650672" question: 'how-context-is-extended producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the second composition PNG. The two declared inputs now converge near the middle of the occupied image rather than forcing Core and the output down onto the lower baseline. The matched connection and extended Context are close together. The green recovery tab is retained in Context before and after binding; Durable remains a separate blue provider. This makes the relevant change a newly bound ability, not creation of a second storage implementation inside Context. The seam now names contract name and version, and the resulting Context explicitly says starting the engine is a separate action. The provider wording explains saving decisions together and one writer instead of relying on writer-fence jargon. The drawing has spare space around a four-object causal explanation, but the earlier stranded provider/bottom-only output arrangement is changed. I can follow which object asks for a capability, which supplies it, and what Core matches. The plug metaphor abbreviates semantic contract matching; it does not prove provider behavior, runtime authority, or readiness. Session and exact reconstruction semantics remain in the referenced design and the companion recovery view. I have not observed a child's comprehension or interest. These are image-located model findings supporting this bounded explanation, not an approval score or a claim that the proposed Module migration is implemented.\n")
 (.o identity: 'reading-3c6a8bc507ae view: 'durable-feature-composition revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-058f60b05522ddf968afe1ccb6e4cba711f3c6a4013e5438c88dfeb52b5ac8b5 image-sha: "3c6a8bc507aeb649e81a65c5bf81cda8c9422225c66c6828851efe01fbdf769b" question: 'how-context-is-extended producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the first composition image. The fitted Recovery tab communicates a Module extension, and the separate Durable journal supplies a contract rather than becoming an internal copy of Context. Needs and offers meet before the extended Context appears. However the lower baseline strongly favors the extension path: the provider is stranded above it and the upper-right area is mostly unused. This is the same spatial weakness the user rejected. The binding and result should be balanced with both converging inputs using reusable native constraints, not case coordinates. Writer fence and contribution vocabulary burden a novice; explain the visible action as one writer and saving decisions together. The plug metaphor must say that contract identity/version is matched, not imply physical connection automatically starts a live owner. The existing phrase runtime handoff still explicit is necessary but technical. These are actual current-model observations, not a pass or an interest score. The reader still has reason to ask which new ability the feature adds and who actually saves the work.\n")
